  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lysine<math><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>Ninhydrin (this is given out by all the amino acids and Lysine is an amino acid.)<br /><br />Furfural<math><mo>&#8594;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthol.</p><p>Rapid furfural test is used to distinguish between glucose and fructose. In this test, the sugar solution is added to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></math>naphthol and concentrated&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.<br /><br />Benzyl alcohol &rarr; ceric ammonium nitrate.<br /><br />Ceric ammonium nitrate test is used for testing of alcohols.<br /><br /><img height=\"83\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7cbb44ab-9605-45ae-9ca1-3a02cb18f82a-image.png\" width=\"128\" /></p><p>Styrene undergoes oxidation when treated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KMnO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>.</p>",
